# @jsr packages are now available on the default npm registry.
# Removed "@jsr:registry=https://npm.jsr.io" because EdgeOne's remote build sandbox
# cannot reach npm.jsr.io, which broke `npm install` of @oak/oak (alias @jsr/oak__oak)
# and made `edgeone makers build` exit 1. npmjs.org mirrors @jsr/*, so this is safe
# for both local and remote builds.
